<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Azariqa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 684–699</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Azariqa were the most militant faction of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kharijites">Kharijites</a>, named after their leader Nafi ibn al-Azraq, who broke away at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basra">Basra</a> around 684. They declared Muslims who did not join them unbelievers and held that their women and children could lawfully be killed. They fought the Zubayrid and Umayyad governors of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> until al-Muhallab ibn Abi Sufra destroyed them around 699.</p></div>
